  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 779a78af73fa30240a0241decfdea172, type: 3}
  voiceSubs:
  - Thou hast done well. Perhaps if things had gone a different way...
  - But no matter. Thou hast but delayed the catastrophe.
  - The Slasher of Veils is already testing its bonds.
  - As thou knowest, my brother has caged it, but unless you stop the beast, the
    havoc it wreaks will be just as bad.
  - As my brother knew, no mortal spell or weapon may harm it.
  - If only my bones could be laid to rest, I might be able to help.
  - Tyball didst not bury me in my grave, but rather hid my bones after he slew me.
  - I suspect they are somewhere below Tyball's caves, in the southwest.
  - Bury them properly in my grave, and many of the shackles on my power will be
    lifted...
  soundSource: {fileID: 0}
